{"id":313,"type":"vertex","label":"hoverResult","result":{"contents":{"kind":"markdown","value":"\n```rust\nstd::collections::hash::map::HashMap\n```\n\n```rust\nimpl<K, V, S, A> HashMap<K, V, S, A>\npub fn get<Q>(&self, k: &Q) -> Option<&V>\nwhere\n    Q: ?Sized,\n    K: Borrow<Q>,\n    Q: Hash + Eq,\n    // Bounds from impl:\n    K: Eq + Hash,\n    S: BuildHasher,\n    A: Allocator,\n```\n\n---\n\nReturns a reference to the value corresponding to the key.\n\nThe key may be any borrowed form of the map's key type, but\n[`Hash`](https://doc.rust-lang.org/stable/core/hash/trait.Hash.html) and [`Eq`](https://doc.rust-lang.org/stable/core/cmp/trait.Eq.html) on the borrowed form *must* match those for\nthe key type.\n\n# Examples\n\n```rust\nuse std::collections::HashMap;\n\nlet mut map = HashMap::new();\nmap.insert(1, \"a\");\nassert_eq!(map.get(&1), Some(&\"a\"));\nassert_eq!(map.get(&2), None);\n```"}}}
